everpure.flasharray 1.46.0, issue #1103 (Everpure-Ansible/FlashArray-Collection): Purity returns
priority_adjustment.priority_adjustment_value = null on every volume of the lab arrays (Purity 6.12.3/6.12.4, REST 2.59);
py-pure-client leaves it unset and reading it raises AttributeError, so purefa_info volumes/vgroups and purefa_volume on
an existing volume fail with "Module failed.". Fixed upstream (commit 333dcca, issue closed 2026-11-05) but in no
release yet. This patch reads the value with getattr(..., None), as the upstream fix does; behaviour is unchanged
when the array returns a value. Generated 2026-11-20 from the installed 1.46.0 files. Applied by docker/eda.Dockerfile
(patch -p1 --forward, the build fails if it does not apply) and checked by docker/check_flasharray_patch.py.
DROP THIS FILE when a release ships the fix (bump docker/requirements.yml, rebuild, rerun the probe).

